TIP:  Tom sharps the last verse but rather than deal with the strange sharped chords I've increased it by a full semi-tone, from (G) to (A) in which you play different, but familiar chords.

TIP:  These are Tom T's original lyrics.  Sometime in the 70s someone got their knickers in a knot  over the reference to "bourbon in a glass and grass" in the second verse so for live performances Tom would sometimes substitute in "old TV shows and snow."

TIP:  For the intro, form the chord and pick the notes (notes may or may not transpose).  Untransposed for up the (G) and pick the strings indicated.  You walk down the strings from 6 to 4, come back up to grab the 5th string again, then walk up the strings beginning with the 3rd string.  Repeat.  Easy.  The sequence repeats in the verse but skip it if you want.  After the key change it forms the coda so hold (A) and do the same sequence but this time you start with the 4th string: 4 - 3 - 2 - 3 - 1 - 2 - 3 - 1. 


